16 0 obj
<</A 57 0 R/Alt(Panel a shows an agricultural orchard with rows of fruit trees bearing red apples and a grassy path between them. Panel b depicts a forestry orchard with wider spaced trees on bare soil and dense foliage.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 32 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

17 0 obj
<</A 58 0 R/Alt(PRISMA-style flowchart illustrating the identification, screening, and inclusion process for a systematic review. Out of 436 records identified from multiple databases with specific search criteria, 73 were excluded by humans, 88 were not retrieved, and 156 were excluded for not being relevant. A total of 119 studies were included in the final review.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 33 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

18 0 obj
<</A 59 0 R/Alt(Diagram compares two fruit detection workflows from orchard images. Traditional image segmentation involves data acquisition, segmentation of images, and detection counting, while the deep learning-based approach uses feature extraction followed by segmentation, detection, and counting for improved identification accuracy.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 34 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

19 0 obj
<</A 60 0 R/Alt(Diagram comparing one-stage and two-stage object detection models on fruit detection. Both models start with an input image of apples on a tree, use feature extraction modules, and output detection results with labeled bounding boxes for fruit categories. The one-stage model directly classifies categories and labels in a single step. The two-stage model first generates suggestions, then refines detections for final category and label outputs.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 37 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

20 0 obj
<</A 61 0 R/Alt(Four images display agricultural vehicle platforms: top left, an autonomous robot car with sensors and a yellow detection field in an orchard; top right, a driverless vehicle scanning plants beside a translucent blue field; bottom left, an orange tracked robot navigating an orange orchard; bottom right, a modified tractor with an extended horizontal bar in a rural setting with parked vehicles nearby.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 47 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

21 0 obj
<</A 62 0 R/Alt(Three labeled drone types are shown. Panel a displays a multi-rotor drone with four arms hovering near a metal tower. Panel b shows a fixed-wing unmanned aerial vehicle with swept-back wings resting on grass. Panel c presents a vertical takeoff and landing fixed-wing drone with two booms and propellers positioned on pavement.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 48 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

22 0 obj
<</A 63 0 R/Alt(Diagram presenting data collection platforms for crop yield estimation, with icons for satellite, unmanned aerial vehicle, and autonomous vehicle around an illustrated fruit tree. Data types shown include RGB, hyperspectral, LiDAR, thermal imaging, and environmental data, processed using machine learning, deep learning, and fusion approaches.)/K 0/P 8 0 R/Pg 50 0 R/S/Figure/T()>>
endobj

